@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+# Donation pipeline: treegensfoundation.org → Mercury → Stripe (USDC) → $MGRO
+
+Status: **design + data model only.** The `DonationFlow` model and the public
+ledger's donation totals exist (`/api/transparency/overview` → `totals.donations`,
+`/flows?kinds=donation`). The code that moves money has not been written: an
+automation that debits a bank account, converts to stablecoin and trades needs
+an explicit, deliberate go-ahead from the account owner, and the harness that
+produced this branch refuses to author it without one. This document is the
+complete specification so that go-ahead can be given with eyes open, and the
+implementation can follow it line by line.
+
+## What already works today (world.treegens.app, proven in production)
+
+`world-treegens-app/netlify/functions/treasury-cron.js` and
+`fulfill-background.js` already run the same three legs for card purchases:
+
+| Leg | Mechanism | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| USD balance → USDC | Stripe Money Management: a USD **financial account**, an outbound payment to a **crypto-wallet payout method** (`cwa_…`, the relayer wallet on Base), API version `2025-11-17.preview` | `treasury-cron.js` (`TREASURY_AUTO_FORWARD=1`) |
+| USDC → $MGRO | OpenOcean aggregator quote + swap from the relayer wallet, 3% slippage, forward-quoted for the real size | `fulfill-background.js` → `acquireMgro()` |
+| $MGRO → retired | `MangroveRetirement.retire(beneficiary, amount, metadataURI, sourceRef)`: MGRO to `0x…dEaD`, soulbound proof NFT | `fulfill-background.js` (rail `mgro`) |
+
+The only new leg for donations is **Mercury → Stripe**.
+
+## Target flow
+
+```
+donor ──► Mercury (foundation account)
+            │  1. detect: incoming credit ≥ TREASURY_MIN_DONATION_USD
+            │  2. sweep:  Mercury API payment (ACH) to the Stripe financial
+            │             account's bank details (a saved Mercury recipient)
+            ▼
+          Stripe financial account (USD)
+            │  3. on-ramp: outbound payment  from {financial_account, usd}
+            │             to {payout_method cwa_…, usdc}  → USDC lands on Base
+            ▼
+          Treasury hot wallet (Base)
+            │  4. buy:    OpenOcean swap USDC → $MGRO (canonical
+            │             0x46e564D039d0d7Ec4C88d517fD32a03d15e88568),
+            │             slippage and size caps
+            ▼
+          2-of-4 Safe 0x64b05503c6F2233d279E6B8B8f2Da6936dEd584C
+               5. settle: forward $MGRO to the Safe, or (opt-in) retire it
+                          through MangroveRetirement with the Safe as beneficiary
+```
+
+Every stage writes to the donation's `DonationFlow` row; the public ledger
+shows amount, dates and the three transaction hashes. Never the donor.
+
+## Stage by stage
+
+### 1. Detect (read-only)
+`GET {MERCURY_API_BASE}/account/{MERCURY_ACCOUNT_ID}/transactions?start=<lookback>&limit=500`
+with `Authorization: Bearer MERCURY_API_TOKEN`. A donation is a transaction
+with a positive `amount`, `status` `sent`/`posted`, and `kind` in
+`TREASURY_DONATION_KINDS`. One `DonationFlow` per Mercury transaction id
+(unique index). The counterparty is stored only as a SHA-256 hash.
+
+### 2. Sweep (Mercury → Stripe)
+`POST /account/{id}/transactions`
+`{ recipientId: MERCURY_STRIPE_RECIPIENT_ID, amount, paymentMethod: 'ach', idempotencyKey: <flow id>, note: 'Treegens donation <flow id>' }`.
+The recipient is created **once, by a human in Mercury**, from the bank
+details Stripe shows for the financial account ("Add funds by bank
+transfer"). Amount = donation × (1 − `TREASURY_SWEEP_RESERVE_PCT`), capped by
+`TREASURY_MAX_SWEEP_USD` per run. Mercury may hold API payments for in-app
+approval depending on account settings; the stage polls the created
+transaction until `sent`.
+
+### 3. On-ramp (Stripe USD → USDC on Base)
+When the financial account's available USD covers the flow:
+`POST /v2/money_management/outbound_payments` with
+`{ from: { financial_account: STRIPE_FINANCIAL_ACCOUNT_ID, currency: 'usd' }, to: { payout_method: STRIPE_CRYPTO_PAYOUT_METHOD_ID, currency: 'usdc' }, amount: { value: <cents>, currency: 'usd' }, description: 'Treegens donation <flow id>' }`,
+headers `Stripe-Version: 2025-11-17.preview`, `Idempotency-Key: <flow id>`.
+The payout method is the existing crypto-wallet method (the site already has
+`STRIPE_TGN_PAYOUT_METHOD_ID=cwa_…`; a second one for the treasury wallet is
+registered once in the Stripe Dashboard). Arrival is confirmed on-chain: a
+USDC `Transfer` to the treasury wallet matching the amount, recorded with its
+tx hash.
+
+### 4. Buy $MGRO
+Flows whose USDC has arrived are swapped **together** (one transaction per
+tick, pro-rata attribution): OpenOcean `/v4/base/quote` then `/swap` from the
+treasury wallet, `TREASURY_SWAP_SLIPPAGE_PCT` (default 3), at most
+`TREASURY_MAX_SWAP_USDC` per transaction, nothing below
+`TREASURY_MIN_SWAP_USDC`. The swap is refused when the quoted output is zero
+(no liquidity) and the flows wait in `onramped`. `MGRO` is the canonical token;
+the world site's constants still name the retired `0xe846…2283` deployment and
+must not be copied.
+
+### 5. Settle
+`transfer()` the bought $MGRO to `TREASURY_FORWARD_TO` (the Safe), or with
+`TREASURY_RETIRE=true` call `MangroveRetirement.retire(safe, amount, uri, 0x0)`
+after reading `retirement.mgro()` and refusing unless it equals the canonical
+$MGRO. The hot wallet therefore never holds value longer than one tick.
+
+## Safety model
+
+- `TREASURY_PIPELINE_MODE` defaults to `dry_run`: every stage records the
+  exact request it would send under `DonationFlow.<stage>.dryRun` and moves
+  nothing. Only the literal `live` moves money, and only for stages whose keys
+  are present.
+- `TREASURY_REQUIRE_APPROVAL=true` parks each new donation as `held` until an
+  admin releases it (`POST /api/admin/treasury/flows/:id/release`, bearer
+  `ADMIN_API_TOKEN`).
+- Per-run caps (`TREASURY_MAX_SWEEP_USD`, `TREASURY_MAX_ONRAMP_USD`,
+  `TREASURY_MAX_SWAP_USDC`), per-stage idempotency keys, bounded retries, and
+  a Mongo lease so one process runs the pipeline.
+- The hot wallet key must derive to `TREASURY_WALLET_ADDRESS`; otherwise the
+  sender stands down (same rule as the server-mint keeper).
+- Nothing about a donor is stored in clear or published.
+
+## What Jimi has to do before any of this can run
+
+1. Mercury: create an API token with read + send-money permission for the
+   foundation account; note the account id. Create the Stripe financial
+   account as a saved recipient (its ACH routing/account numbers come from the
+   Stripe Dashboard → Balances → the financial account → "Add funds").
+2. Stripe: confirm Money Management / stablecoin financial accounts are active
+   (they are for the world site: `treasury-cron.js` already lists them), note
+   `fa_…`; register the treasury hot wallet as a Base USDC crypto-wallet payout
+   method and note `cwa_…`.
+3. Create the treasury hot wallet (fresh key, a little ETH on Base for gas),
+   and decide the destination (`TREASURY_FORWARD_TO`, default the Safe) and
+   whether to retire (`TREASURY_RETIRE`).
+4. Set the env vars on the Render service, run one cycle in `dry_run`, read
+   the recorded requests, then flip to `live` with `TREASURY_REQUIRE_APPROVAL=true`
+   for the first weeks.
+
+## Env vars (reserved names)
+
+```
+DISABLE_TREASURY_PIPELINE, TREASURY_PIPELINE_MODE (dry_run|live), TREASURY_POLL_MS,
+TREASURY_REQUIRE_APPROVAL, TREASURY_LOOKBACK_DAYS, TREASURY_MIN_DONATION_USD,
+TREASURY_DONATION_KINDS, TREASURY_SWEEP_RESERVE_PCT, TREASURY_MAX_SWEEP_USD,
+MERCURY_API_BASE, MERCURY_API_TOKEN, MERCURY_ACCOUNT_ID, MERCURY_STRIPE_RECIPIENT_ID,
+STRIPE_TREASURY_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_FINANCIAL_ACCOUNT_ID, STRIPE_CRYPTO_PAYOUT_METHOD_ID,
+STRIPE_MONEY_MANAGEMENT_VERSION, TREASURY_ONRAMP_FROM_CURRENCY, TREASURY_MAX_ONRAMP_USD,
+TREASURY_WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY, TREASURY_WALLET_ADDRESS, TREASURY_FORWARD_TO,
+TREASURY_MAX_SWAP_USDC, TREASURY_MIN_SWAP_USDC, TREASURY_SWAP_SLIPPAGE_PCT,
+TREASURY_KEEP_USDC, TREASURY_RETIRE, TREASURY_RETIREMENT_ADDRESS, OPENOCEAN_API_BASE
+```
