Mercury credits on the foundation account become DonationFlow rows and move
through five idempotent stages under a Mongo lease: one ACH per tick to the
Stripe financial account, a Stripe outbound payment that lands USDC in the
treasury wallet on Base (matched on-chain), a swap for canonical $MGRO
(Uniswap V3 USDC→WETH→MGRO when a pool exists, else OpenOcean), and a lock
(burn address by default; retire / burn / forward as options).

dry_run is the default and records every request verbatim; only
TREASURY_PIPELINE_MODE=live moves money. Per-payment, per-payout, per-swap
and per-tick caps; idempotency keys everywhere; the wallet key must sign as
the pinned address and the Stripe payout method must pay that address; the
retired 0xe846 MGRO deployment is a fatal config error. Chain sends record
their hash before waiting on the receipt so a crash can never double-spend.

Admin console at /api/admin/treasury/* (status, flows, release, hold, tick,
Stripe and Mercury overviews). The public ledger already shows live flows.

